Exp29: REJECTED. Exp27 untouched.

Exp30 result — D1 bullish continuation context as conditional exit-side modulator: REJECTED under the frozen EXIT_WEIGHTED whole-day criterion. Frozen flag was Track-D bias_sign=+1 AND point-in-time broker-day daily_direction=BULLISH AND 0.70<=D1Position<0.90 AND 09:00<=state_time_BRT<=18:00. Sample was small at realized exits (TRAIN 40, VALIDATION 16, TEST 17 flagged exits). TRAIN fitted k_side=-0.606936484 (odds multiplier 0.545018), but the sign did not transport: VALIDATION observed ADVANCE|EXIT=18.75% vs BaseQ=10.91% while the negative TRAIN coefficient pushed ExtQ down to 7.36%; TEST observed=23.53% vs BaseQ=27.86% and ExtQ=21.80%. Primary EXIT_WEIGHTED gains: VALIDATION Brier -0.001263513 CI[-0.004943629,+0.001214549], LogLoss -0.004871202 CI[-0.014889987,+0.002802275]; TEST Brier -0.000177646 CI[-0.002655674,+0.002026869], LogLoss +0.000641127 CI[-0.004953512,+0.005794916]. Strict pass=False. P(EXIT) invariance and unflagged-state invariance both held to floating-point precision. No alternate D1 bands, bearish mirror, extreme-zone rescue, continuous D1 or Track-A/Z/Fib/Scale/HMM/Energy rescue. Runtime promotion: NONE.

Interpretation: the previously observed D1 0.70-0.90 bullish 120m continuation context does not transport as a one-parameter modifier of P(ADVANCE|EXIT) inside the active-frontier structural state machine. This does not erase the older D1-context result because the estimands and conditioning sets differ materially.

Exp31 frozen next question — open Track B MULTI-DAY DNA with a simple, isolated sequence baseline rather than further mining Track-D integrations. Use completed M5 broker-days strictly before the Exp27 shadow start; drop first and last broker-day to avoid partial-edge days. One row = one completed broker-day target. Define day_sign=sign(close-open). For target day d, y_continue=1 if sign_d == sign_{d-1}; Streak2=1 if sign_{d-1} == sign_{d-2}, using previous observed completed broker-days only. BASE is TRAIN constant continuation probability. EXTENDED keeps BASE intercept frozen and fits exactly one TRAIN coefficient k_streak2 applied only when Streak2=1; Streak2=0 predictions remain identical. Primary estimand=DAY_WEIGHTED; dependence-aware uncertainty=resample whole ISO broker-weeks while preserving day weights. Survival requires Brier and LogLoss gain CI95>0 in both Validation and TEST. UP-streak and DOWN-streak are diagnostics only and cannot rescue failure. No streak-length 3/4 search, weekday filters, D1 zones, Clock, Z, Fib, Track-D state, thresholds or interactions. Repeatedly inspected historical OOS remains exploratory; runtime promotion NONE.